  "name": "Koo.éex' song (Tlingit memorial-party song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ceremonial song of the Tlingit of southeast Alaska, sung at the koo.éex', the memorial party or potlatch at which clans display their crests and sing clan-owned mourning songs and dance songs to frame drums, represented here by the generic frame-drum card. Louis Shotridge recorded Tlingit songs on wax cylinders for the University of Pennsylvania Museum, and the biennial Celebration organised by Sealaska Heritage Institute in Juneau now gathers Tlingit, Haida and Tsimshian dance groups.",
